# torchfits: backport of upstream CFITSIO develop commits
#   bd8d127e4d9be83c149e0e7f92faac02ab2cc947 (2026-08-27)
#     "Add a divide by zero check."
#   85bc354010ca18ea62bee6731a25d43e6c1b5c55 (2026-10-01)
#     "Added another divide-by-zero check to decode()."
#   b07f2e4c0881d88a329765f1552580065ac50c71 (2026-11-02)
#     "Added bounds checking of input (compressed) memory array throughout
#      hdecompress. This includes a change to the signature of the two
#      hdecomp functions present in fitsio.h"
#
# The H-compress decoder read the compressed tile with no length at all: a
# truncated or corrupt HCOMPRESS_1 tile read past the heap buffer that holds
# it, and an image header with ny == 0 divided by zero (SIGFPE on x86). The
# decoder now takes the tile length and fails with DATA_DECOMPRESSION_ERR.
# torchfits reaches it on every read of an HCOMPRESS_1 tile-compressed image.
#
# fits_hdecompress / fits_hdecompress64 gain an `long insize` parameter, as
# upstream. torchfits does not call them directly; imcompress.c is their only
# caller in the vendored tree. Upstream's follow-up 077a024 only updates its
# unit tests (not vendored here). The three commits rewrite the same lines,
# so they are one patch: the net diff from cfitsio-4.7.0 to b07f2e4.
#
# Drop this patch when extern/VERSIONS.txt moves to a CFITSIO release that
# contains these commits.

